      "writtenOn": "2021-07-13T04:16:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a good question. Checked the data sheet. These GPIOs are powered by V_HIF. When the V_HIF supply is 1.8V, the signal levels match 1.8V. It is not configurable, like switching between 3.3V and 1.8V. There is no Low-Voltage GPIO Control register for these GPIOs.\n\nThe EC-OS gpio.inc:\n   ALTERNATE(PIN_MASK(4, 0xC0), 1, MODULE_SPI, GPIO_SEL_1P8V)\n   ALTERNATE(PIN_MASK(5, 0x28), 1, MODULE_SPI, GPIO_SEL_1P8V)\n\nactually does nothing, as no mapping to a valid Low-Voltage GPIO Control register. I will remove the GPIO_SEL_1P8V flag from the gpio.inc config.",
      "parentUuid": "de393651_b2938bbf",
